The main method is Resolve(), and ResolveUtc() does the work. ResolveUtc() converts the server time to UTC, reads the clock of the reset zone, and picks the date on which the current day started. It then checks that candidate against the boundaries on both sides. A reset time inside a skipped hour moves by one hour, and the first guess can be a day off. Resolve() converts the two boundaries to server clock readings.
