The start and end of a day are server clock readings. The elapsed time from the start to the end is not always 24 hours. When the reset zone changes its clock inside a day, the day is 23 or 25 hours long. A clock change of the server zone alone does not change the length, because it moves only the server readings of the two boundaries.
My first version of the length method subtracted the two server readings, and it reported 24 hours for every day, including the short and long ones. My second version converted both server readings back to UTC. A later check showed that it still gave 23 hours for a day whose end falls into the hour that the server clock shows twice. That reading was converted as its first instant, one hour too early. The version below takes both boundaries in UTC from ResolveUtc() and does not go through the server clock at all.
