The fit reads the server clock through the trading schedule. An early close, a holiday, a missing bar, or a special session moves the last bar of a week. A few such weeks in the same season could look like another DST rule, above all in a short history. The class does not tell a schedule effect from a clock effect. The class reports the weeks that the best zone does not explain, and the user has to look at those weeks.
The bars are not the only source. After the fit, FitServerClock.mq5 waits for a new tick and takes its server time minus the UTC clock of the computer. That reading does not use the bars, so it can confirm or reject the fitted offset of that day. It says nothing about the rule, and it depends on a correct computer clock.
